    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To move from 2NF to 3NF, you need to eliminate transitive dependencies. A transitive dependency occurs when a non-key attribute depends on another non-key attribute, instead of directly on the primary key. Identify these \"A $\\rightarrow$ B, B $\\rightarrow$ C\" chains where A is the key, and move the dependent attributes (C, in the example) into a new, separate table linked back to the original one. This ensures that every non-key attribute depends only on the whole key and nothing else.",
